    "result_text": "All 42 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the three new `Cp29Tests` and every existing checkpoint. The suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, city-validated `postcode` field for owners across the full stack:\n\n**1. API contract \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\nAdded an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`, not in `required`). Because `Owner` is `allOf: OwnerFields`, it's both accepted on create and returned on read. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with `postcode` accessors at build time.\n\n**2. Domain \u2014 `Owner.java`**\nAdded the `postcode` field with `@Column(name = \"postcode\")` plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions (name match), so no mapper change was needed.\n\n**3. Persistence \u2014 `schema.sql` (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql)**\nAdded a `postcode` column to the `owners` table. The tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in SQL. The hsqldb `data.sql` uses positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, so I inserted a `NULL` postcode value into each of the 10 seed rows to keep the column counts aligned (h2/postgres/mysql already use explicit column lists).\n\n**4. Validation \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`**\nAdded `validatePostcode(postcode, city)`, called after the required-fields check:\n- `null` postcode \u2192 accepted (backward-compatible, optional-when-absent).\n- Present \u2192 must be exactly 4 digits, else `400` (`InvalidFieldsException`).\n- Range-checked against the city's region via fixed tables (`Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099`); out-of-range \u2192 `400`.\n- A city with no known region has no range \u2192 any 4-digit postcode accepted.\n\nOne bug I caught during testing: `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE (immutable maps reject `null` lookups), which fired for the random unlisted cities the tests use. I fixed it by resolving the region first and short-circuiting to no range check when it's `null`.\n\nI scoped this to the create path, matching the checkpoint spec and tests (which exercise create only); `updateOwner` follows the existing minimal pattern and wasn't in scope.",
